<title>USA: 1st Source to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>1st Source to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH BEND, Ind. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1st Source Corp said Friday its board of directors approved the repurchase of up to 10 percent of its outstanding common stock, or 1,560,000 shares.</p>
<p>The company said the purpose of the buyback is to provide common stock for its employee benefit plans and for stock dividends and splits.  The stock purchases will be made on the open market when favorable conditions exist, it added.</p>
<p>1st Source is a banking holding company with assets of $2.11 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
